{"format":"floorplan/1","building":"OLYMPIC","floor":"1","title":"Olympic Hall floor 1","extent":"full","source":{"publisher":"UCLA Housing","what":"Olympic Hall level 1 plan (CAD export) from UCLA Housing's room sign-up map site","url":"http://www.housing.ucla.edu/maps/plans/Olympic-01.htm","file":"http://www.housing.ucla.edu/maps/plans/Olympic/O-01.png","index":"https://housing.ucla.edu/my-housing/maps-and-tours/housing-building-maps -> http://www.housing.ucla.edu/maps/","date":"2021-04-02 (file date)","accessed":"2026-10-15"},"how":"Walls are the dark lines of the plan image; rooms are the spaces they enclose, with door gaps closed by extending each wall end up to 2 m. The plan has no scale or north arrow, so its building outline was fitted to the mapped outline (scale, rotation and shift, by iterative closest point).","notes":["Plan: UCLA Housing's CAD export of Olympic Hall level 1 (room sign-up map, file dated 2021-04-02). Walls are its dark lines (gray level below 150); the furniture is drawn lighter and is left out. Room numbers are the plan's labels (O101...); the tracer stores the leading letter O as a zero (0101), which the site's room-key normalisation reads as 101.","Georeference: the plan footprint (the L-shaped wing plus the study-commons tower) is fitted to the mapped outline by ICP, with the same 20 degree rotation on every floor; orientation checked on floors 2 and 4 with UCLA GIS restrooms (OH227/OH262, OH427/OH456), which fall on the plan's all-gender restrooms. The housing site's north arrow (north up-left) agrees.","The exterior walls are drawn as light glazing in places, so rooms along them leaked to the outside; cuts along the mapped outline (the L wing and the tower) seal them. The outline's north block (the makerspace / upper-floor housing bar) is not cut.","Study rooms, lounges and other spaces the plan labels by name only (OPEN STUDY, GROUP STUDY, LOUNGE...) carry that name; the site's room numbers (375B/C/D, 470, 475) are not printed on 